# The small fixes (docs/steps/small-fixes/answered.md): tests that no
# longer depend on chance, each shown to bite. The sandbox watch's time
# bound, tested with a time of zero now that the tests that need a whole
# look give it a time no machine reaches; and the change detector's cap on
# git, tested with a git that never answers.

# From mutations/small-fixes-git-cap.breaks (part `git-cap`).
# The small fixes: a git that has not answered when the change detector's
# cap passes is not waited for. The test's git never answers, so a look that
# waits for it is a test that runs out of time.

# ------------------------------------------- git is not waited for past its cap

[break] a-brief-answer-is-waited-for-past-its-limit
rule: A brief program that has not answered when its limit passes is killed, and its answer is not waited for.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/process/brief.rs
in: answer
find: receiver.recv_timeout(limit)
replace: receiver.recv().map_err(|_| mpsc::RecvTimeoutError::Disconnected)
caught-by:
    cineris-tools::it changes::sys_git_that_does_not_answer_in_time_is_not_waited_for

[break] the-looks-cap-is-not-gits-limit
rule: Git, asked what changed, is waited for no longer than the look's cap.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/changes.rs
in: ChangeDetector::git
find: brief::answer(child, self.cap)
replace: brief::answer(child, self.cap + Duration::from_secs(3600))
caught-by:
    cineris-tools::it changes::sys_git_that_does_not_answer_in_time_is_not_waited_for

# From mutations/small-fixes-sandbox-watch.breaks (part `sandbox-watch`).
# The small fixes, the sandbox watch's part: the time bound of
# the look at protected paths, tested with a time of zero, which stops
# every look on any machine, now that the tests that need a whole look give
# it a time no machine reaches.

# ------------------------------------------------- a look past its time

[break] a-look-ignores-its-time
rule: A look that has taken its time stops at its next check and says it is incomplete; a time of zero stops it at the first.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/protect.rs
in: Look::out_of_time
find: self.started.elapsed() >= self.limits.time
replace: false
caught-by:
    protect::tests::past_its_time_a_look_says_it_is_incomplete

[break] a-look-out-of-time-says-it-is-complete
rule: A look that stops for its time says it is incomplete, so that what lay beyond where it stopped is not reported as made or gone, and the user is told the look was made in part.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/protect.rs
in: Look::out_of_time
find: self.complete = false;
replace: return true;
caught-by:
    protect::tests::past_its_time_a_look_says_it_is_incomplete
